      "knowledge_point": "Calculating the Complex Conjugate of a Complex Matrix",
      "problem": "Find $B=\\overset{―}{A}$, where $A=[\\begin{aligned}7-\\text{i} & 6+4\\text{i} \\\\ 7-4\\text{i} & 4+9\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].$ What is the value of ${b}_{12}-{b}_{21}?$",
      "worked_solution": "Taking the complex conjugate of each entry, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{A} & =\\overset{―}{[\\begin{aligned}7-\\text{i} & 6+4\\text{i} \\\\ 7-4\\text{i} & 4+9\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{7-\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{6+4\\text{i}} \\\\ \\overset{―}{7-4\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{4+9\\text{i}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7+\\text{i} & 6-4\\text{i} \\\\ 7+4\\text{i} & 4-9\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${b}_{12}-{b}_{21}=(6-4\\text{i})-(7+4\\text{i})=-1-8\\text{i}.$",
