      "problem": "Find $B=\\overset{―}{A}$, where $A=[\\begin{aligned}5+4\\text{i} & -6\\text{i} \\\\ -5+7\\text{i} & 8-3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].$ What is the value of ${b}_{21}-{b}_{22}?$",
      "worked_solution": "Taking the complex conjugate of each entry, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{A} & =\\overset{―}{[\\begin{aligned}5+4\\text{i} & -6\\text{i} \\\\ -5+7\\text{i} & 8-3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{5+4\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{-6\\text{i}} \\\\ \\overset{―}{-5+7\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{8-3\\text{i}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5-4\\text{i} & 6\\text{i} \\\\ -5-7\\text{i} & 8+3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${b}_{21}-{b}_{22}=(-5-7\\text{i})-(8+3\\text{i})=-13-10\\text{i}.$",
