      "problem": "Find the imaginary part of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1-7\\text{i} & 2-4\\text{i} \\\\ 6\\text{i} & -5\\end{aligned}].$",
      "worked_solution": "For the given matrix $A,$ we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1-7\\text{i} & 2-4\\text{i} \\\\ 6\\text{i} & -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1-7\\text{i} & 2-4\\text{i} \\\\ 0+6\\text{i} & -5+0\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -5\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Re}(A)}+\\text{i}{{[\\begin{aligned}-7 & -4 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Im}(A)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{Im}(A)=[\\begin{aligned}-7 & -4 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{aligned}].$",
