    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-76201",
      "knowledge_point_id": "3c28b8ae-71ef-5d26-895a-5d949fc5b164",
      "knowledge_point": "Computing Components of the Real and Imaginary Parts of a Complex Matrix",
      "problem": "If $\\,\\text{Re}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,\\text{Im}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}e & f \\\\ g & h\\end{aligned}]\\,$ are the real and imaginary parts of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}2-3\\text{i} & 1-\\text{i} \\\\ 1+\\text{i} & 5\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]\\,$ then what is the value of $cd+gh?$",
      "worked_solution": "For the given matrix $A,$ we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}2-3\\text{i} & 1-\\text{i} \\\\ 1+\\text{i} & 5\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2-3\\text{i} & 1-\\text{i} \\\\ 1+\\text{i} & 0+5\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Re}(A)}+\\text{i}{{[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Im}(A)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $c=1,d=0,g=1$ and $h=5.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\ncd+gh=1\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 5=5.\n$$",
