    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-38390",
      "knowledge_point_id": "3c28b8ae-71ef-5d26-895a-5d949fc5b164",
      "knowledge_point": "Computing Components of the Real and Imaginary Parts of a Complex Matrix",
      "problem": "If $\\,\\text{Re}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,\\text{Im}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}e & f \\\\ g & h\\end{aligned}]\\,$ are the real and imaginary parts of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}3+5\\text{i} & -2-4\\text{i} \\\\ 2-3\\text{i} & 1-6\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]\\,$ then what is the value of $ad+eh?$",
      "worked_solution": "For the given matrix $A,$ we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}3+5\\text{i} & -2-4\\text{i} \\\\ 2-3\\text{i} & 1-6\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Re}(A)}+\\text{i}{{[\\begin{aligned}5 & -4 \\\\ -3 & -6\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Im}(A)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $a=3,d=1,e=5$ and $h=-6.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\nad+eh=3\\cdot 1+5\\cdot (-6)=-27.\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
