      "knowledge_point": "Multiplying Complex Matrices",
      "problem": "If $\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}2-\\text{i} & 3+\\text{i} \\\\ 1+2\\text{i} & 1+\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}1+\\text{i} & 2+\\text{i} \\\\ -2+\\text{i} & 1-\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]\\,$, then $AB=$",
      "worked_solution": "Multiplying the matrices using the usual method, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}2-\\text{i} & 3+\\text{i} \\\\ 1+2\\text{i} & 1+\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1+\\text{i} & 2+\\text{i} \\\\ -2+\\text{i} & 1-\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}(2-\\text{i})(1+\\text{i})+(3+\\text{i})(-2+\\text{i}) & (2-\\text{i})(2+\\text{i})+(3+\\text{i})(1-\\text{i}) \\\\ (1+2\\text{i})(1+\\text{i})+(1+\\text{i})(-2+\\text{i}) & (1+2\\text{i})(2+\\text{i})+(1+\\text{i})(1-\\text{i})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}(3+\\text{i})+(-7+\\text{i}) & 5+(4-2\\text{i}) \\\\ (-1+3\\text{i})+(-3-\\text{i}) & 2+5\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4+2\\text{i} & 9-2\\text{i} \\\\ -4+2\\text{i} & 2+5\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
