      "math_academy_id": "q-76211",
      "knowledge_point_id": "83fad21d-6b36-5198-a13f-362d34342475",
      "knowledge_point": "Multiplying Complex Matrices",
      "problem": "If $\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}3+\\text{i} & -\\text{i} & 1-4\\text{i} \\\\ 1-\\text{i} & 1+\\text{i} & 2\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}1+\\text{i} \\\\ 1-\\text{i} \\\\ 1+4\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]\\,$, then $\\,Ax=$",
      "worked_solution": "Multiplying the matrix by the vector using the usual method, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax & =[\\begin{aligned}3+\\text{i} & -\\text{i} & 1-4\\text{i} \\\\ 1-\\text{i} & 1+\\text{i} & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1+\\text{i} \\\\ 1-\\text{i} \\\\ 1+4\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}(3+\\text{i})(1+\\text{i})+(-\\text{i})(1-\\text{i})+(1-4\\text{i})(1+4\\text{i}) \\\\ (1-\\text{i})(1+\\text{i})+(1+\\text{i})(1-\\text{i})+2(1+4\\text{i})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}(2+4\\text{i})+(-\\text{i}-1)+17 \\\\ 2+2+(2+8\\text{i})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}18+3\\text{i} \\\\ 6+8\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
