    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-76223",
      "knowledge_point_id": "83fad21d-6b36-5198-a13f-362d34342475",
      "knowledge_point": "Multiplying Complex Matrices",
      "problem": "If $\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}1-3\\text{i} & -1+2\\text{i} \\\\ 2+2\\text{i} & 1-\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}3-\\text{i} & 3+\\text{i} \\\\ -1+\\text{i} & 1-\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]\\,$, then $AB=$",
      "worked_solution": "Multiplying the matrices using the usual method, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}1-3\\text{i} & -1+2\\text{i} \\\\ 2+2\\text{i} & 1-\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3-\\text{i} & 3+\\text{i} \\\\ -1+\\text{i} & 1-\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}(1-3\\text{i})(3-\\text{i})+(-1+2\\text{i})(-1+\\text{i}) & (1-3\\text{i})(3+\\text{i})+(-1+2\\text{i})(1-\\text{i}) \\\\ (2+2\\text{i})(3-\\text{i})+(1-\\text{i})(-1+\\text{i}) & (2+2\\text{i})(3+\\text{i})+(1-\\text{i})(1-\\text{i})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-10\\text{i}+(-1-3\\text{i}) & (6-8\\text{i})+(1+3\\text{i}) \\\\ (8+4\\text{i})+2\\text{i} & (4+8\\text{i})+(-2\\text{i})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1-13\\text{i} & 7-5\\text{i} \\\\ 8+6\\text{i} & 4+6\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
