    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-140381",
      "knowledge_point_id": "ef2e7753-83f4-5826-a04f-89616d34c578",
      "knowledge_point": "Applying Row Operations to a Complex Matrix",
      "problem": "Given the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1+2\\text{i} & -2-4\\text{i} \\\\ 3-2\\text{i} & \\text{i}\\end{aligned}]$, find the result of applying to $A$ the following  elementary row operations:\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}=\\frac{1}{1+2\\text{i}}{R}_{1},\\,{R}_{2}={R}_{2}+(2\\text{i}-3){R}_{1}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's apply the row operations to $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1+2\\text{i} & -2-4\\text{i} \\\\ 3-2\\text{i} & \\text{i}\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{1+2\\text{i}}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 3-2\\text{i} & \\text{i}\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(2\\text{i}-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 6-3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the result is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 6-3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3\\text{i}-3\\end{aligned}]",
              "option": "0",
              "source_option": "a"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2-3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]",
              "option": "1",
              "source_option": "b"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 6-3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]",
              "option": "2",
              "source_option": "c"
            },
