      "knowledge_point_id": "ef2e7753-83f4-5826-a04f-89616d34c578",
      "knowledge_point": "Applying Row Operations to a Complex Matrix",
      "problem": "Given the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}2-\\text{i} & 2\\text{i}+1 \\\\ 3\\text{i} & -2\\end{aligned}]$, find the result of applying to $A$ the following elementary row operation:\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-\\frac{3\\text{i}}{2-\\text{i}}){R}_{1}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's apply the row operations to $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}2-\\text{i} & 2\\text{+}1 \\\\ 3\\text{i} & -2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-\\frac{3\\text{i}}{2-\\text{i}}){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2-\\text{i} & 2\\text{i}+1 \\\\ 3\\text{i}+(-\\frac{3\\text{i}(2-\\text{i})}{2-\\text{i}}) & -2+(-\\frac{3\\text{i}(2\\text{i}+1)}{2-\\text{i}})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2-\\text{i} & 2\\text{i}+1 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{(-4+2\\text{i})+(6-3\\text{i})}{2-\\text{i}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2-\\text{i} & 2\\text{i}+1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the result  is \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2-\\text{i} & 2\\text{i}+1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
